  "title": "Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.100",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Suppose that $A$ and $G$ are finite groups such that $A$ acts coprimely on $G$ by automorphisms. Let $C=C_G(A)$ be the fixed-point subgroup, and let $C'$ denote its derived subgroup. Is it true that the number of $A$-invariant irreducible characters $\\chi$ of $G$ whose restriction $\\chi_C$ is never zero is exactly $|C/C'|$?",
